{"name":"Earthquake","hex":"#8c7553","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"earthquake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shaking of the ground, caused by volcanic activity or movement around geologic faults. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Such a quake specifically occurring on the planet Earth, as opposed to other celestial bodies."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To undergo an earthquake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earthquake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Earthquake","blocks":[{"text":"An earthquake, also called a quake, tremor, or temblor, is the shaking of the Earth's surface resulting from a sudden release of energy in the lithosphere that creates seismic waves. Earthquakes can range in intensity, from those so weak they cannot be felt, to those violent enough to propel objects and people into the air, damage critical infrastructure, and wreak destruction across entire cities. The seismic activity of an area is the frequency, type, and size of earthquakes experienced over a particular time. The seismicity at a particular location in the Earth is the average rate of seismic energy released per unit volume."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Quake_epicenters_1963-98.png/330px-Quake_epicenters_1963-98.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthquake","wikidata":"Q7944"},{"title":"Earthquake (1974 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Earthquake is a 1974 American disaster film directed and produced by Mark Robson, from a screenplay by George Fox and Mario Puzo. The plot concerns the struggle for survival after a catastrophic earthquake destroys most of Los Angeles. It stars an ensemble cast of well-known actors, including Charlton Heston, Ava Gardner, George Kennedy, Lorne Greene, Geneviève Bujold, Richard Roundtree, Marjoe Gortner, Barry Sullivan, Lloyd Nolan, Victoria Principal, Pedro Armendáriz Jr., and Walter Matthau."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Earthquake_movie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthquake_(1974_film)","wikidata":"Q500280"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Kluft-photo-Carrizo-Plain-Nov-2007-Img_0327.jpg/500px-Kluft-photo-Carrizo-Plain-Nov-2007-Img_0327.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Kluft-photo-Carrizo-Plain-Nov-2007-Img_0327.jpg/1280px-Kluft-photo-Carrizo-Plain-Nov-2007-Img_0327.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Kluft-photo-Carrizo-Plain-Nov-2007-Img_0327.jpg/500px-Kluft-photo-Carrizo-Plain-Nov-2007-Img_0327.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial photo of the San Andreas Fault in the Carrizo Plain, northwest of Los Angeles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKluft-photo-Carrizo-Plain-Nov-2007-Img_0327.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/HotelSanSalvador.jpg/330px-HotelSanSalvador.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/HotelSanSalvador.jpg/330px-HotelSanSalvador.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Collapsed Gran Hotel building in the San Salvador metropolis, after the shallow 1986 San Salvador earthquake","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHotelSanSalvador.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Kahramanmara%C5%9F_after_7.8_magnitude_earthquake_in_T%C3%BCrkiye_5.jpg/500px-Kahramanmara%C5%9F_after_7.8_magnitude_earthquake_in_T%C3%BCrkiye_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_